<p>U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said the United States is “not disputing” a joint assessment by five European governments that Russian opposition leader Alexei Navalny was fatally poisoned with a rare toxin linked to poison dart frogs. Rubio added that Washington has “no reason to question” the findings. The European statement—issued by the United Kingdom, France, Germany, the Netherlands, and Sweden—said their analyses pointed to the frog-derived toxin epibatidine and blamed Russia for its use. Russia rejected the allegation, according to reports.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/cZmNM_ks26gTIvcD87KLMPFXAbScspGxlbwisPoYJ43ti49Gbqa_bUib9I_N40gtXBRtvdIC2ZEiYdvxfgCVpOkmNbLHwa4hBRSLVt-7ZNi0BCp6g2UXvGxt7_uHPwLkmTjfzUEXi063kfMHOdX6AuT704hpu5M6DaE8eCQCV2cbO1PS4G8WLC_EEy3uBoXsxovX3B1lBX90TDuJxTiUSbNq9K-OdIGgnrgQ28PU1iZHfBw1qYbAjIoo9v9LSe-ALFuOapgC-J3ylkuXzJuIj67lM4Mrf_g61oBVzgkumWDeM6pYsIKW1g4vvCtmv-5Q8wEqRpKkGjeVT6_GpJLfjz74hs-3IIlV-B7G7m1wCw4ANqVd_9EawHdKkgBAlPZ1Q8JhgdFDEadu0U8sMlLkW2vyrrUQknklMq7AaQaP14k2zONW9Tx82RODpfPpC0dfGM7zHyO9neTZ--uBTU-bgf91wts7VyPerg' alt='U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio speaks to reporters during his Central Europe trip.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Why no US signature: Rubio said the five European governments coordinated the statement themselves, and stressed that the U.S. not signing “doesn’t mean we disagree with the outcome”.</li><li>No rift with partners: Rubio said Washington wasn’t going to “do a fight” with European governments over their assessment.</li><li>UK sanctions review: Britain said it is weighing new sanctions on Moscow after the European assessment.</li><li>Trip itinerary: Rubio started a two-day visit to Slovakia and Hungary, looking to strengthen ties with the two EU countries.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. State Department (Rubio): Rubio said the U.S. has no reason to question the European findings and would not “fight” partners over their conclusion, while explaining the Europeans coordinated their own statement. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/marco-rubio-alexei-navalny-vladimir-putin-kremlin-poisoning/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Five European governments: The U.K., France, Germany, the Netherlands and Sweden said their analyses showed Navalny was poisoned with a toxin from a poison dart frog. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/marco-rubio-alexei-navalny-vladimir-putin-kremlin-poisoning/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Russian government: Moscow dismissed the accusation that Navalny was poisoned, according to reports summarizing the reaction. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/marco-rubio-alexei-navalny-vladimir-putin-kremlin-poisoning/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>United Kingdom: Britain said it was considering new sanctions on Russia after the report. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3343650/us-not-disputing-troubling-european-report-navalny-poisoning-rubio-says'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-not-disputing-european-report-on-navalny-poisoning-rubio-11007718#publisher=newsstand'>US &#x27;Not Disputing&#x27; European Report On Navalny Poisoning: Rubio</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/marco-rubio-alexei-navalny-vladimir-putin-kremlin-poisoning/'>Rubio calls report on Navalny poisoning ‘troubling’</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/rubio-says-us-is-not-disputing-navalny-poisoning-assessment-by-europeans/article70635959.ece'>Rubio says U.S. is not disputing Navalny poisoning assessment by Europeans</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3343650/us-not-disputing-troubling-european-report-navalny-poisoning-rubio-says'>Rubio says US not disputing report of Navalny’s fatal poisoning by frog toxin</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-us-does-not